rince is a beast when these two  Outsiders change each other's lives true  love grows and appearances don't matter  isn't that sweet we love the story but  what we really love about this movie is  the interior design of the cast  Lumiere and all of the other pieces of  furniture that are alive might have  something to do with it after all who  wouldn't love talking to furniture but  since we can't have that we will work  with the next best thing  this bedroom took a page from the  ballroom scene in the movie the colorful  walls and faux stained-glass windows  make us feel like we are in the castle  the lovely ruffled bedspread is just  like Bell's iconic dress this other  bedroom is located in one of Tokyo's  Disneyland hotels it looks like this is  inspired by Belle's library we love that  the furniture totally looks like it  could come to life there are even roses  on the headboard and Lumiere and  Cogsworth in the bookshelf all we need  is a ton of books Toy Story Playhouse as  kids we always wanted our toys to come  to life and be able to reenact the  stories we imagined in our heads Disney  and Pixar's hit Toy Story lets us live  out our dreams with The Adventures of  Woody Buzz and all of the other toy  friends Andy's room was always something  we wanted from the cloud wallpaper to  all the fun toys he had this next  bedroom is actually a playroom which is  totally fitting considering the  inspiration for this it's Toy Story this  amazing playroom is part of a Disney  cruise ship we have never wanted  anything more than to set sail and hang  out in Andy's room look at these amazing  colors the entire room looks like it's  made up of giant toys so if you've ever  wondered what it's like to be one of  buzz and Woody's pals this is your  chance  slinky serves as the slide and they even  have the cloud wallpaper in the  background you can see ham and mr.  Potato Head Andy's bed serves as an  upper level playing area we wonder if  Buzz is waiting to show us how he can  fly The Lion King The Lion King is a  movie blasting with gorgeous color and  memorable characters Simba's adventure  as a young cub and later as an adult  lion made us want to visit the pride  lands and the jungle much like Simba's  transition into adulthood  we have to grow up too but as adults how  do we incorporate our love of Disney  without seeming too childish  we definitely  want to let go of our favorite films  especially this one we can try  decorating our rooms like this  sophisticated individual did they  created an elegant Sahara landscape  inspired by Simba's home they kept the  color palette monochromatic focusing on  warm tones like deep oranges yellow  brown and tans the furniture is simple  and classy the bedding is animal print  which is a fun way to include the  animals from the film the room is  completed with a Simba plush and there  is mosquito netting on the windows and  curtains that look like canvas tents the  nightstands even resemble travel  suitcases and the lats are camping  lanterns how amazing and classy is this  room Peter Pan speaking of flying let's  talk about our favorite flyer Peter Pan  the eternal youth who teaches us to  believe in magic and fairies also taught  us how to fly all you need is a little  faith trust and pixie dust and you're  ready to soar we would love to visit  Neverland and hang out with Tinker Bell  and Peter but they haven't shown up in  our room yet so we have to settle for  bringing the magic to our rooms that's  exactly what this creative person did  here we have a Peter Pan inspired  bedroom with an elegant twist although  Peter Pan is about never growing up this  bedroom is classy and sophisticated we  love the clean look and simplicity of  this room the clean lines and curves of  the furniture are very stylish the blue  and orange are a lively pop of color the  painting of Peter Wendy John Michael and  Tinkerbell flying over London and across  the big bin is amazingly detailed it's  not overwhelmingly themed but still  enough to inspire us just look at the  hot air balloon chandelier it's so  beautifully crafted this room is a great  example of how to do Disney for adults  what a great balance of modern classical  and Disney styles princesses we know  sometimes making choices is difficult  and when it comes to Disney movies there  is no exception there are so many great  stories we can't imagine having to  choose one so what do you do when you  want to decorate your room but can't  decide what to pick well why not choose  a little bit of everything if you love  all of the Disney Princesses  we suggest incorporating them in  your room just like some of these  creative people this person decided to  make one of their walls  a mural including various princesses we  love the patterns and bright colors in  each princess panel they kept the focus  on the princesses by making the  furniture and bedding white and free of  patterns a bold choice we also love this  other bedroom that used Ariel in  Cinderella their mural of the castle and  courtyard made us fill this bedroom is  part of a spectacular castle especially  with Ariel and Cinderella waiting  outside by the fountain the detail in  the brick includes hints of purple and  pink  this colorful masterpiece looks like it  could be a still frame from an actual  Disney movie we love the creativity  frozen frozen took the world by storm in  2013 lucky for us the cold never  bothered us anyway the film features  Princess Anna and her sister Queen Elsa  who accidentally freezes her kingdom  with her powers the lovely story of  sisterly love  combined with catchy songs and beautiful  animation is enough to solidify its  place in Disney history the design of  the film is mostly a beautiful winter  wonderland consisting of lots of blues  and purples naturally this inspired mini  frozen themed bedrooms some included  scenes of the landscape on their walls  as well as the characters such as Elsa  Anna and Olaf other bedroom was went  with a subtle approach and stuck to a  blue color and white color palette  sprinkling snowflake decor on the walls  we loved all of the different ways this  movie has inspired the decor of bedrooms  picking white furniture is a good way to  stay versatile while keeping the winter  theme the blues White's pinks and  purples are a fun way to play around  with accent colors around the room  weather subtle or full-blown we just  need our very own little Olaf and we are  ready to let it go Alice in Wonderland  there are many wonderful Disney films to  draw inspiration from if you are a big  fan of color texture and crazy patterns  then look no further than Alice in  Wonderland  this movie is filled with whimsical  inspiration  Barry Blair was the concept artist for  the film and she did amazing work here  is a bedroom inspired by the film and  just like Mary's work it's hard not to  be inspired this designer certainly took  Alice's adventurous spirit and went with  it there are so many patterns and colors  here from the flowers to the bold prints  on the bedding and the mushrooms even  the tree that Alice falls into is  incorporated into the bed and how cool  are these beanbag chairs made to look  like stones the flower pillows blend  perfectly with the flowers painted on  the wall if you look closely you can see  Alice the Hatter and the Cheshire Cat  hanging out by the flower bed this  beautiful forest really captures the fun  and brightness of Alice in Wonderland  let's just hope the Red Queen doesn't  show up and threatens to take our heads  Cinderella when we watch Disney  Cinderella all we really want is a fairy  godmother to make our dreams come true  Cinderella is the hopeful girl who  dreams of escaping her evil stepmothers  grasp after having her plans and dress  ruined by her stepmother and stepsisters  Cinderella is visited by her fairy  godmother and bibbidi-bobbidi-boo a  little magic and Cinderella is able to  go to the ball her glittering dress and  gorgeous glass slippers had us wishing  for our own transformation and if  Cinderella taught us one thing it's to  dream since a dream is a wish your heart  makes why not turn your sleeping area  into something magical if your room is  looking a little like Cinderella before  the magic why not take a little  inspiration from the princess herself  this gorgeous Cinderella inspired  bedroom is giving us major fields the  absolutely magical landscape of the  castle on the wall makes us feel like we  are in a fairy tale the beautiful  bedding is basically Cinderella's dress  and we are obsessed the attention to  detail in the bedding is exquisite from  the ruffles to the color and the  butterflies all that is missing are the  glass slippers and our own pumpkin  carriage pumpkin carriage speaking of  Cinderella's carriage how cool would it  be to have one of those I'm  imagine having a pumpkin transform into  a sweet ride in front of your eyes that  would be something to see  of course Cinderella's dress and shoes  were necessary for the princess  transformation but one of the coolest  changes that happened was the pumpkin  the elegant round carriage was the  finishing touch on Cinderella's princess  transformation we all wished we could  ride it everywhere but would you want to  sleep in it some creative designers took  the carriage and let it inspire them  this Cinderella carriage themed room is  enough to make us feel like we are being  whisked away to our castles the white  and gold carriage looks almost exactly  like the one in the movie we love the  pop of blue in the bedding and curtains  inside it reminds us of Cinderella's  dress there is even a wishing well and a  faux cobblestone path we are totally  loving the wide open fields painted on  the wall it's almost like looking out  into our own kingdom now all we need are  some horses and we're ready for  dreamland which of these gorgeous rooms  was your favorite let us know in the  comments section below if you'd like to  see more videos like this one then don't  forget to subscribe to our Channel  thanks for watching  [Music]  you  [Music]

